\begin_layout Plain Layout
The expected 
\series bold
square
\series default
 of the modified (by 
\begin_inset Formula $f_{t}$
\end_inset

) output (of 
\begin_inset Formula $\Delta W_{t}$
\end_inset

) equals the 
\series bold
linear
\series default
 integral of the output's modification's square.
\end_layout

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
In a way,
 the 
\begin_inset Formula $\Delta W_{t}^{2}$
\end_inset

 collapses inside the integral to 
\begin_inset Formula $\Delta t$
\end_inset

,
 while the 
\begin_inset Formula $f^{2}$
\end_inset

 multiple remains as a squre.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
This peculiar fact carries the name 
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

Ito's Isometry
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

 (for the very special case of simple functions).
\end_layout

